# PYTHONUNBUFFERED so stdout logs stream to Railway in real time.
#
# --workers: the coordinator was CPU-bound on a single process. Measured, one
# heartbeat costs 6.63ms just to verify its signature, so one core saturates at
# ~151 beats/sec of signature work alone — and the network generates ~44/sec
# alongside every other request. One process could not keep up, which is why
# indexes and caches raised the ceiling without ever reaching it.
#
# Multiple workers are only safe because epoch settlement now takes a Postgres
# advisory lock per run (epoch.py::_cluster_singleton): exactly one worker
# settles an epoch, the rest return immediately. Two settling at once would
# double-credit operators and build two transactions with the same nonce on the
# publisher key.
#
# UVICORN_WORKERS is exported, not just interpolated, because db.py divides the
# connection-pool budget by it — otherwise N workers would open N times the
# connections and Postgres would refuse them.
#
# --limit-concurrency bounds the queue so a slow patch cannot become the
# congestive collapse it caused before: past the cap uvicorn returns 503 without
# invoking the app, costing no worker thread and no pool connection.
web: PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 UVICORN_WORKERS=${UVICORN_WORKERS:-4} uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port ${PORT:-8000} --workers ${UVICORN_WORKERS:-4} --limit-concurrency ${UVICORN_LIMIT_CONCURRENCY:-100}
